    <div class="principles">
      <div class="principle cream"><span class="pn">P.01</span><h4>Calm over noise</h4><p>One canvas, three surface levels, no pure white and no pure black. Colour is a signal budget: amber means money or attention, coral means blocked, everything else stays neutral until proven otherwise.</p></div>
      <div class="principle"><span class="pn">P.02</span><h4>Data first, chrome second</h4><p>Numbers are the product. Numerals run light-weight and tabular at display sizes; labels stay small and quiet. If a decoration competes with a figure, the decoration loses.</p></div>
      <div class="principle"><span class="pn">P.03</span><h4>Motion is orientation</h4><p>Animation only explains where things came from and went: panels slide from their edge, pills glide to the active tab, presses scale to 96.5%. Nothing bounces for fun. GPU transforms only.</p></div>
      <div class="principle"><span class="pn">P.04</span><h4>Accessible by construction</h4><p>AA contrast on all text pairs, visible keyboard focus, 36px minimum targets, <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> honoured globally. A state that cannot be perceived by keyboard or screen reader does not exist.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subhead"><h3>General usage rules</h3><span class="hint">How the system is applied</span></div>
    <div class="cols2">
      <div class="ddodont">
        <div class="dd do"><h5><span class="statedot" style="background:#7BB694"></span> Do</h5>
          <ul>
            <li>Compose screens from <b>Card</b> primitives (<code>plain</code>, <code>cream</code>, <code>flat</code>) on the shared canvas gradient.</li>
            <li>Reserve <b>cream cards</b> for KPI / hero moments — max two per viewport.</li>
            <li>Use token names in code and Figma alike: <code>--am-500</code>, not “that yellow”.</li>
            <li>Keep one <b>primary (dark) action</b> per surface; everything else is soft or ghost.</li>
            <li>Round everything on the radius scale; pills for controls, 24px for cards, 28px for modals.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dd dont"><h5><span class="statedot" style="background:#E8503F"></span> Don’t</h5>
          <ul>
            <li>Don’t introduce pure <code>#fff</code> / <code>#000</code> fills — surfaces are always translucent.</li>
            <li>Don’t use coral decoratively; it is reserved for blocked states and unread signals.</li>
            <li>Don’t invent shadows or blurs — pick an elevation level (DS-03).</li>
            <li>Don’t set body copy below 12.5px or above 45 characters per line in panels.</li>
            <li>Don’t title-case buttons, tabs or card titles. Sentence case everywhere.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="note" style="background:var(--surface-cream)">
        <b>Reading order.</b> Work top-to-bottom: primitives (01–03) define raw values, usage (04) defines behaviour, components (05) are the shipped set, screens (06) show composition. Anything not covered here is undefined — raise a token request instead of improvising.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="subhead"><h3>Contribution flow</h3><span class="hint">From gap in the system to shipped token</span></div>
    <div class="flowsteps">
      <div><b>Propose</b>Open a token request with the failing use-case and a screenshot of the current workaround.</div>
      <div><b>Review</b>Design-eng triages weekly; duplicates merge into the nearest existing token.</div>
      <div><b>Ship</b>Token lands in <code>index.css</code> + this board in the same PR, versioned as minor.</div>
      <div><b>Deprecate</b>Removed tokens stay one release with a <code>@deprecated</code> comment and migration note.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

