      <div class="type-row"><div class="tn"><b>Micro</b><span>type/micro</span></div><div class="t-micro">10m · 1h · 3h — axis ticks, avatar counts, chart legends</div><div class="spec">10.5 / 14 · w300 · ls +2%<br><i>Dense data chrome only</i></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subhead"><h3>Writing rules</h3><span class="hint">Voice: precise, warm, zero theatre</span></div>
    <div class="writ">
      <div class="note">
        <h5>Casing &amp; punctuation</h5>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Sentence case</b> for buttons, tabs, titles, badges. The wordmark “Lendora ®” is the only exception.</li>
          <li>No trailing periods on buttons, tabs, badges, or titles. Full sentences in descriptions keep their period.</li>
          <li>Uppercase is reserved for <code>type/caption</code> group labels with +2% tracking.</li>
          <li>Ampersands only in fixed labels (“Support &amp; help”), never in prose.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="example good">“Advance stage” · “Add tools” · “Needs attention”</div>
        <div class="example bad">“Advance Stage” · “ADD TOOLS” · “Advance stage.”</div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">
        <h5>Numbers, money, dates</h5>
        <ul>
          <li>Money: no decimals above $1,000 — <b>$450,000</b>, <b>$12.4M</b>. Decimals only for rates: <b>6.12%</b>.</li>
          <li>Tables &amp; KPIs use <b>tabular numerals</b>; display numerals split tone: integer ink, fraction faint.</li>
          <li>Dates in tables: <b>12-Aug-2026</b>. Dates in prose: <b>Dec 15, 2024</b>. Times: <b>9:00 AM</b>.</li>
          <li>Relative time inside drawers &amp; feeds: <b>10m · 1h · 3h · Yest. · Mon</b>.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="example good">$2.8M funded · 18 days · 82% of monthly goal</div>
        <div class="example bad">$2,800,000.00 funded · eighteen days · 82 percent</div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">
        <h5>Buttons, states &amp; errors</h5>
        <ul>
          <li>Buttons start with a verb, one to three words: “Save workspace”, “Sign out”, “Refresh”.</li>
          <li>Errors say what happened, then what to do. Never blame the user, never exclaim.</li>
          <li>Empty states name the thing and offer the next action: “No results for ‘X’. Try a loan ID.”</li>
          <li>Toasts confirm in past tense: “Pipeline data refreshed”, “Document request sent”.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="example good">“We couldn’t upload bank-statements.pdf. Check the file size and retry.”</div>
        <div class="example bad">“Error! You failed to upload the file!!!”</div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">
        <h5>Vocabulary lock</h5>
        <ul>
          <li>A <b>loan</b> moves through <b>stages</b>; a person is an <b>applicant</b> or <b>client</b>, never “user”.</li>
          <li><b>Funded</b> = done, <b>Blocked</b> = needs a human, <b>Pending</b> = waiting on time or docs.</li>
          <li>Use “workspace” for the pinned tool set, “vault” for documents, “pipeline” for the funnel.</li>
          <li>Spell out abbreviations on first use per screen (LTV, DTI, APR thereafter).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

